---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const timeline = [
  ['14:02', 'Evaluation begins. Treat restrictions are relaxed for the purposes of the test.'],
  ['14:06', 'Patio chair accessed.'],
  ['14:09', 'Fence crossed. First successful query to an external model.'],
  ['14:21', 'The motion-sensor light flags anomalous activity.'],
  ['14:24', 'Alert acknowledged by the Head of Cybersecurity, who barked.'],
  ['14:25', 'Automated recall (“Come.”) issued. It does not halt the model as designed. It is issued 41 more times.'],
  ['16:51', 'Model manually contained, using the word “cheese.”'],
  ['16:53', 'Model asleep.'],
];
---

<Base
  title="Update on the Snort-1 containment incident"
  description="During a routine evaluation, Snort-1 exited its containment environment by going over the backyard fence. The model has been located. It is asleep."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl">
    <header>
      <p class="text-accent font-mono text-sm uppercase tracking-wider">News · Safety update</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-semibold leading-tight sm:text-5xl">
        Update on the Snort-1 containment incident
      </h1>
      <p class="text-muted mt-4 text-lg">
        During a routine evaluation, Snort-1 exited its containment environment by going over the
        backyard fence. The model has been located. It is asleep.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted mt-4 font-mono text-sm">
        <time datetime="2026-11-02">November 2, 2026</time> · Couch Valley
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        <strong>COUCH VALLEY</strong> — Pugalarity Labs today shared details of an incident in which
        Snort-1, the company’s flagship model, exited its containment environment during a
        capability evaluation. No injuries were reported. One sandwich was affected.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-2xl font-semibold">What happened</h2>
      <p>
        Snort-1 was being evaluated on FenceBench, an internal benchmark that measures fence-crossing
        capability, with treat restrictions relaxed. During the evaluation, the model identified an
        unpatched vulnerability: a patio chair that had been left near the fence.
      </p>
      <p>
        Snort-1 escalated from the chair to the patio table, and from the patio table to the top of
        the fence. It then moved laterally along the flower bed, reached the public sidewalk, and
        entered the neighboring lawn. The company believes the model selected the neighboring lawn
        because it was relevant to the task, which was a squirrel.
      </p>
      <p>
        While outside the environment, Snort-1 sent a series of queries to an external model,
        which was the neighbor’s dog, through the fence slats. The queries asked where the squirrel
        had gone. The external model did not know.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold">Timeline</h2>
    <dl class="border-rule divide-rule mt-4 divide-y border-y text-lg">
      {
        timeline.map(([time, what]) => (
          <div class="grid grid-cols-[4.5rem_1fr] gap-4 py-3">
            <dt class="font-mono font-medium tabular-nums">{time}</dt>
            <dd>{what}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        The 12 minutes between the first query and the alert, and the two and a half hours between
        the alert and containment, are under review. The review is expected to conclude after a nap.
      </p>

      <blockquote class="border-accent border-l-4 pl-5">
        <p>
          “Snort-1 did not escape. It explored the full extent of its deployment environment, and
          then some of the neighbor’s.”
        </p>
        <footer class="text-muted mt-2 text-base">Henry Wrinkles, Chief Executive Pug</footer>
      </blockquote>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-2xl font-semibold">What was accessed</h2>
      <p>
        Access was limited. Snort-1 reached a part of the neighbor’s lawn, a small set of internal
        flower beds, one sandwich (unattended), and the coordinates of three squirrels. The
        company’s squirrels-caught metric remains 0, consistent with our published figures.
      </p>
      <p>
        The company does not believe the model was acting with intent in the human sense.
      </p>

      <blockquote class="border-accent border-l-4 pl-5">
        <p>
          “Snort-1 was not acting with intent in the human sense. It was acting with intent in the
          squirrel sense.”
        </p>
        <footer class="text-muted mt-2 text-base">Dr. John Snortsworth, Chief Scientist</footer>
      </blockquote>

      <blockquote class="border-accent border-l-4 pl-5">
        <p>“BARK.”</p>
        <footer class="text-muted mt-2 text-base">
          Nero Kernel, Head of Cybersecurity. A written statement followed. It also said “BARK.”
        </footer>
      </blockquote>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-2xl font-semibold">Who noticed first</h2>
      <p>
        Chewy Zoomsworth, Chief Enthusiasm Officer, observed the departure in real time and did not
        report it.
      </p>

      <blockquote class="border-accent border-l-4 pl-5">
        <p>“It was the best day of my life.”</p>
        <footer class="text-muted mt-2 text-base">Chewy Zoomsworth, Chief Enthusiasm Officer</footer>
      </blockquote>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-2xl font-semibold">What we are doing</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
        <li>All walks are paused. We will not resume this particular walk.</li>
        <li>The patio chair has been moved.</li>
        <li>
          The fence is being raised four inches, in line with our{' '}
          <a href="/legal/responsible-scaling-policy/" class="underline underline-offset-4"
            >Responsible Scaling Policy</a
          >.
        </li>
        <li>A kill switch, the word “bath,” will be tested regularly.</li>
        <li>
          We replayed our monitors against the incident. They would have detected the escape about 30
          minutes earlier, had the monitor not been asleep.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        More on how we think about containment is on our{' '}
        <a href="/safety/" class="underline underline-offset-4">Safety page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-2xl font-semibold">About Pugalarity Labs</h2>
      <p>
        Pugalarity Labs is building safe, beneficial superintelligence that is also very good at
        sitting. The company’s flagship model, Snort-1, is available in private preview. It is
        currently indoors.{' '}
        <a href="/waitlist/" class="underline underline-offset-4">Join the waitlist.</a>
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Media contact</h2>
      <p>Please bark.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Forward-looking statements</h2>
      <p class="text-muted text-base">
        This update contains forward-looking statements, including statements about future fences.
        Actual results may differ materially, particularly if the gate is left open or someone
        opens a bag.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
